definitions-set.jsonl — provenance and licence

This fixture is this repository's own work: 100 "what is X" questions,
authored in-repo, licensed under this repository's own MPL-2.0. It is not a
redistribution of any external question set.

Each question's gold answer was checked against the Open English WordNet's
own hypernym labels (CC-BY-4.0; see corpus/wordnet/LICENSE-NOTICE for the
full attribution). Checking gold labels against WordNet's data does not make
this file a WordNet derivative — no WordNet text is copied into it — but a
reader should know where the "is this term answerable" boundary comes from:
the corpus band's gold phrase is the corpus's own label for that term, so the
delta this fixture measures is how much of the corpus's own knowledge the ask
grammar can already reach, not independent world knowledge held outside it.

Selection rule (three bands, 100 questions, follow this when adding rows):

  - seed (20 rows): the term already carries a clean, single /r/IsA row in
    corpus/tier2/human.jsonl, so the question is answerable before AND after
    the wordnet-xl import. This keeps the "before" score honestly nonzero
    instead of measuring a fixture that starts at zero by construction.
  - corpus (70 rows): the term is absent from corpus/tier2/human.jsonl but
    carries a single, clean /r/IsA row in corpus/wordnet/wordnet-xl.jsonl.
    This is the band the delta actually measures. Selected from wordnet-xl's
    own IsA rows where both sides are a single token and the subject is a
    word a general reader recognises; nouns preferred. A term whose subject
    also carries a verb-sense hypernym in wordnet-xl (trumpet -> utter,
    taxi -> locomote, oak -> wood are three found this way) is rejected even
    if a noun-sense row is the more natural read, because the ask grammar has
    no way to prefer one sense over another.
  - neither (10 rows): the term is absent from every corpus this rig can
    reach, so the question stays a miss before and after the import. This
    band is the visible ceiling: a fixture tuned only to the delta would
    score 100 after the load, which would hide the fact that most of the
    world stays outside what any shipped corpus can ground.
